    "summary": "Monumental Dark Star/Eyes → China Doll suite and tight, energetic set flow",
    "blurb": "The concert features a soaring Dark Star → Eyes Of The World → China Doll stretch anchored by Jerry's gritty solos and Phil's deep bass work. Row Jimmy and Playing In The Band stand out as tight, high‑energy numbers. Overall the setlist flows smoothly with consistently high energy.",
    "review": "February 15, 1973 at the Dane County Coliseum captures the Dead in top form during a classic early‑'70s run. After a lively first set that builds from Loose Lucy through Row Jimmy and a seamless China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue, the band launches into a second‑set centerpiece: a 45‑minute Dark Star → Eyes Of The World → China Doll suite that showcases Jerry’s country‑flavored phrasing, Phil’s “Phil zone” bass marathon, and Bill’s immaculate tom work. Highlights like Playing In The Band, Here Comes Sunshine and the tight rhythm on Bertha keep the momentum high, while Donna’s vocal presence adds texture throughout. The recording quality is excellent in several soundboard sources—especially gd1973-02-15.sbd.hall.1580.shnf—and a crystal‑clear matrix tape further emphasizes the show’s dynamic range, making this night a must‑listen for any Deadhead.",
